  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1039 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nTuesday will likely be our warmest day, as afternoon temperatures\nreach the mid to upper 90s and heat indices peak at 105+ in many \nareas. Thus, it is quite possible that a Heat Advisory will be \nneeded for Tuesday, and Tuesday only. At this time, the \natmospheric models are bringing a surface boundary through the mid\nstate late Tuesday that would bringing nominally cooler \ntemperatures, and also lower humidity. It also appears that the \nfropa would be a dry one except for a spotty shower or two. In \nfact, after Saturday night, our rain and storm chances for the \nremainder of the 7-day forecast period look to be negligible.",
